    "body": "Work towards enabling [\"flow\" layout](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/9244da12e400ec0291450a5e9400d995e7a29b83/src/gen/gen_help_html.lua#L86-L88) in all `:help` files.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nThe final boss of vimdoc pseudo-structure: Vim's quasi-headings on function signatures and excmd docs is visually distinctive but too inconsistent for a nice parse rule.\r\n\r\n\r\n    \t\t\t\t\t\t\t*:ve* *:ver* *:version*\r\n    :ve[rsion]\t\tPrint editor version and build information.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n- Define the quasi-heading format as an \"h4\" variant, specified at `:help help-tag-heading`.\r\n  - For simplicity and predictability, it is defined as any line that ends with a help tag(s) preceded by 2 or more spaces (or 1 tab).\r\n- Update existing docs.\r\n  - This one-time update has a lot of changes, but is very unlikely to conflict with ported Vim-patches because (1) Vim rarely adds new *excmds* that we want, and (2) *function* docs are auto-generated.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n    :ve[rsion]\t\t\t\t\t\t*:ve* *:ver* *:version*\r\n    \t\t\tPrint editor version and build information.\r\n\r\nref https://github.com/neovim/tree-sitter-vimdoc/issues/110",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-17T15:34:03Z",
